# Project Principles

- Build the smallest complete system that satisfies the assessment well.
- Prefer clarity, correctness, maintainability, and testability over cleverness.
- Keep implementation aligned with `docs/requirements.md`.
- Do not add technologies unless they directly improve the assessment outcome.
- Keep business logic out of UI components, route handlers, and migration files.
- Document important trade-offs where reviewers will benefit from the reasoning.
- Use incremental commit messages after major steps, but only commit when asked.
- Treat salary data as sensitive: validate inputs, avoid leaking internals, and keep logs useful but non-sensitive.
